# 🚨 Common JFrog + GitHub Actions Docker Errors (And How to Avoid Them)

> A practical guide to avoid hours of debugging when pushing Docker images to JFrog Artifactory.

---

## ❌ Error #1: `Wrong username was used`

### 🔴 Error Message

```
unknown: Wrong username was used
```

### ❌ Root Cause

Using **email ID** instead of **JFrog username** during Docker login.

JFrog Docker registry **does not always accept email IDs**.

### ✅ Correct Fix

Use **JFrog username**, found in:

```
JFrog UI → Profile → Username
```

### ✅ Correct Login

```bash
docker login <domain>.jfrog.io
Username: jfrog_username
Password: access_token
```

---

## ❌ Error #2: `invalid reference format`

### 🔴 Error Message

```
invalid tag "***/docker-local/springboot:latest": invalid reference format
```

### ❌ Root Cause

Incorrect Docker image tag due to **wrong JFrog URL** or **secret masking**.

Most common mistake:

```
https://trialoan6sj.jfrog.io
```

Docker expects:

```
trialoan6sj.jfrog.io
```

### ✅ Correct JFrog URL

```
trialoan6sj.jfrog.io
```

✔ No `https://`
✔ No `/artifactory`
✔ No `/api/docker`

---

## ❌ Error #3: Using Artifactory API URL for Docker Login

### 🔴 Wrong Value

```
https://<domain>.jfrog.io/artifactory/api/docker/docker-local
```

### ❌ Why This Fails

Docker **does not authenticate via REST APIs**.

Docker only communicates with:

```
https://<domain>.jfrog.io/v2/
```

### ✅ Correct Registry Host

```
<domain>.jfrog.io
```

---

## ❌ Error #4: Multiline `docker build -t \` Breaks in GitHub Actions

### 🔴 Problematic YAML

```yaml
docker build -t \
${{ secrets.JFROG_URL }}/docker-local/app:latest .
```

### ❌ Why It Breaks

* Line breaks + secret masking
* Produces invalid image names (`***`)

### ✅ Best Practice Fix

Use shell variable:

```yaml
IMAGE_NAME=${{ secrets.JFROG_URL }}/docker-local/app:latest
docker build -t $IMAGE_NAME .
```

---

## ❌ Error #5: JFROG_URL Secret Masked as `***`

### 🔴 Log Output

```
IMAGE_NAME=***/docker-local/app:latest
```

### ❌ Root Cause

Secret contains invalid characters or URL format.

### ✅ Correct Secret Value

```
JFROG_URL=trialoan6sj.jfrog.io
```

Delete and re-add the secret if needed.

---

## ❌ Error #6: `unauthorized: authentication required`

### 🔴 Root Cause

* Used JFrog password instead of **Access Token**
* Token expired or revoked

### ✅ Fix

Generate token:

```
Profile → Security → Access Tokens
```

Use token as Docker password.

---

## ✅ Final Golden Rules (Save This)

| Rule         | Always Remember                 |
| ------------ | ------------------------------- |
| JFrog URL    | `<domain>.jfrog.io`             |
| Username     | JFrog username ≠ email          |
| Password     | Access Token only               |
| Repo Type    | Docker → Local                  |
| Image Format | `<domain>/<repo>/<image>:<tag>` |
| Never use    | `/artifactory/api/docker`       |

---

## 🏁 Example of Correct Setup

```bash
docker login trialoan6sj.jfrog.io
docker build -t trialoan6sj.jfrog.io/docker-local/springboot-app:latest .
docker push trialoan6sj.jfrog.io/docker-local/springboot-app:latest
```

